WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.187
The Frame Card outcome names a user, a workflow,
its current condition, a desired condition, a

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:07.814
metric, and constraints.

00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:09.697
Co-author it with the operator.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:14.183
Use a measure the operator recognizes
and define its denominator.

00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:18.435
Separate desired outcome from the
technology proposed to achieve it.

00:00:18.505 --> 00:00:21.982
A frame that says deploy
AI specifies a solution.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:27.471
A frame that says reduce review time while
preserving routing quality leaves room to choose

00:00:27.541 --> 00:00:29.717
the simplest useful intervention.

00:00:29.787 --> 00:00:35.205
The fictional baseline is a median of 20
minutes across twelve simulated reviews.

00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:41.761
The team proposes a median no greater than 14
minutes for an equivalent assisted sample, with

00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:44.263
at most one misroute per twelve decisions.

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:48.130
These are exercise thresholds
agreed before reading results.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.979
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:53.049 --> 00:00:57.870
Write the outcome line and define review
time, sample size, and routing error.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:04.127
For support agents, improve ticket review from
a median of 20 to at most 14 minutes, measured

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:09.957
on twelve comparable simulated tasks, while
keeping human approval and no more than one wrong

00:01:10.027 --> 00:01:15.509
queue. Review time starts when the reviewer
opens the ticket and ends at a saved decision.

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:20.529
Wrong queue means disagreement with the
case reference label after adjudication.

00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:22.732
Which frame preserves solution choice?

00:01:22.802 --> 00:01:24.893
A. Deploy an AI agent B.

00:01:24.963 --> 00:01:28.611
Reduce defined review time
under quality constraints C.

00:01:28.681 --> 00:01:30.174
Use the newest model.

00:01:30.244 --> 00:01:31.716
The best answer is B.

00:01:31.786 --> 00:01:34.922
An outcome frame allows competing interventions.
